# Pao on a composite yakuman (Daisangen + Tsuuiisou) won by 3rd-party ron
# (engine.md §4.2 Pao, rules.md §1 pao_composite_yakuman, pao_ron_split, §4.31).
# Honba: 1.
# Seat 1 pons 5z (from S0), 6z (from S3), and 7z (from S2 -> sets Daisangen pao on Seat 2!),
# holding 111z 2z (all honors -> Daisangen + Tsuuiisou = 2x Yakuman, 64000).
# Seat 3 (3rd party) discards 2z -> Seat 1 rons 2z!
# - Mahjong Soul: Daisangen (32000) split 50/50 between liable Seat 2 (16000 + 300 honba = 16300)
#   and discarder Seat 3 (16000); Tsuuiisou (32000) paid normally by discarder Seat 3!
#   Totals: Seat 2 -16300, Seat 3 -48000, Seat 1 +64300.
# - Tenhou: Whole composite hand (64000) split 50/50 between liable Seat 2 (32000 + 300 honba = 32300)
#   and discarder Seat 3 (32000)!
#   Totals: Seat 2 -32300, Seat 3 -32000, Seat 1 +64300.

[meta]
name: pao_composite_yakuman_ron
title: Composite yakuman third-party ron splits only liable yakuman on Mahjong Soul and whole hand on Tenhou
rules: both
source: engine.md §4.2, rules.md §1, §4.31
unverified: rules.md §5 item 12 (no discriminating composite pao payment)

